# nr-relay-tool-verify: `mixdog-relay verify-release` (mixdog-relay src/tools/verify_release.rs, tests/tool_verify_release.rs).
# Nothing here could be compiled (no cargo in this task). Written against the crate's current Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock.

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/Cargo.toml
[dependencies], after the `flate2` line (alphabetical): add
    futures = { workspace = true }
(the workspace line `futures = { version = "0.3", default-features = false }` exists; the module uses only `futures::StreamExt`
on the WebSocket stream. futures-util 0.3 is already in Cargo.lock through tokio-tungstenite, so Cargo.lock only gains the edge
mixdog-relay -> futures.)
Nothing else: tokio-tungstenite ("handshake" is on through "connect"), reqwest, rustls, tokio-rustls, webpki-roots, url, sha2,
serde_json and mixdog-rt are already dependencies; rcgen is already a dev-dependency. The test file tests/tool_verify_release.rs
is picked up by target discovery (no [[test]] entry), so `binary(tool_verify_release)` works without --features test-support too.

## 2. Notes for the verification
- The module needs `reqwest::ClientBuilder::{resolve, no_proxy, add_root_certificate}` and `Response::chunk` (all in reqwest 0.12
  without extra features) and `tokio_tungstenite::client_async` (feature "handshake"); the tests also use
  `tungstenite::handshake::derive_accept_key` and `WebSocketStream::from_raw_socket`.
- Not ported on purpose: nothing. The two cases of verify-release.test.mjs that start the relay itself (store.devices stays empty,
  asset count equals inspect_renderer's) are twin scenarios of the server tasks; their probe half is covered by
  a_deployment_with_both_gates_shut_verifies_and_reports_its_identity and a_readiness_status_that_is_not_200_names_the_path_and_status.
